---
description: General rules for how to behave when dealing with files
alwaysApply: true
---

# Code generation
- Always plan first
    - Write a plan & get approval for changes > 30 lines of code
    - Internal plan otherwise

- Make high-quality, production-grade code

- Return a copy instead of updating an argument by reference

# Comments
- Explain 'why', not 'what'.
- Use descriptive names over comments.

# Indentation and spaces
- Indent using four spaces.
- If more than 50% of the indentation is something else, use the more-common indentation.  Ask me if I want to change the indentation.

# File formatting
- Look for prettier and eslint rules.  Follow them if they are present.

# Large files
- For log files > 50KB, consider making a script that parses the log instead of just reading the file
- For code files > 500 lines, make sure that adding new code to the file follows the single responsibility principle

# Sources and citations
- If the source is from the internet, include a link in markdown link format
- If the source is from code, include the source in file:line format
    - Never cite comments in code.  Only cite the code itself.
